In the context of hierarchical deterministic (HD) wallets, the coin type (*coin type* in English) is a derivation level that makes it possible to differentiate the wallet's branches according to the different cryptocurrencies used. This derivation level, defined by BIP-0044, is located at depth 2 of the derivation structure, after the master key and the purpose (*purpose*). For example, for Bitcoin, the assigned index is `0x80000000`, noted `/0'/` in the derivation path. This means that all addresses and accounts derived from this path are associated with Bitcoin. This derivation level makes it possible to properly separate the different assets in a multi-currency wallet. Here are the indexes used for different cryptocurrencies:
* Bitcoin: `0x80000000`;
* Bitcoin Testnet: `0x80000001`;
* Litecoin: `0x80000002`;
* Dogecoin: `0x80000003`;
* Ethereum: `0x8000003c`...

![BIP-84 tree with an arrow pointing to the Coin Type level (m/84'/0'), which identifies the targeted cryptocurrency.](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/LoicPandul/Dictionnaire-de-Bitcoin/bab568e32351cc9f1240f49f5feedc242123d101/definitions/fr/t/type-de-devise/assets/image-1.png)
